+///     only size where one source pixel is one square block of four.
+///   - **Stretched**, a GB or GBC picture scales until it fills the panel's
+///     height: 3.889x, so 622x560 with 65px of paper a side. Nothing is
+///     cropped and the aspect is right.
+///   - **GBA is never stretched.** `source_rect` returns `WHOLE_TEXTURE` for it
+///     in both modes, so stretch is already a no-op upstream, and the largest
+///     aspect-correct fit here would be 3.133x -- non-integer pixels for 4%
+///     more picture, which is a bad trade nobody asked for.
+///
+/// Two sizes that were tried on the device and rejected, so they do not come
+/// back: filling the whole 752x560 (21% wider than square pixels, which is
+/// what "stretch" meant for a day) and a whole 4x at 640x560, which is uniform
+/// and 2.9% bigger than the above but crops 2 source rows off the top and 2
+/// off the bottom. The crop was the part nobody liked.
+pub fn base_size(platform: Platform, mode: VideoMode) -> [f32; 2] {
